The following three conditions on a ring $A$ are equivalent:
(a) every ideal in $A$ is finitely generated;
(b) every ascending chain of ideals $\mathfrak{a}_1 \subset \mathfrak{a}_2 \subset \dots$ eventually becomes constant, i.e., $\mathfrak{a}_m = \mathfrak{a}_{m+1} = \dots$ for some $m$;
(c) every nonempty set of ideals in $A$ has a maximal element.
